§ `Article 11 -- graduated retirement benefit (src:138-142)`

-- (1): 17.83 pence is increased by 3.8 per cent and the reference is to 18.51 pence
#ASSERT `art 11(1): section 36(1) of the National Insurance Act 1965, the sum of graduated retirement benefit, in pence` EQUALS `the pair of sums in the arts 8-19 tests` 17.83 18.51
-- (2) to (4): each sum "shall be increased by 3.8 per cent"
#ASSERT `art 11(2): the increase for deferred retirement after the increase of 3.8 per cent` 100 EQUALS 103.8
#ASSERT `art 11(3): the lump sum after the increase of 3.8 per cent` 1000 EQUALS 1038
#ASSERT `art 11(4): the addition for widows and widowers after the increase of 3.8 per cent` 200 EQUALS 207.6
#ASSERT `art 11(2) to (4): the sum after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `an increase of graduated retirement benefit for deferred retirement (Schedule 2 to the 1978 Regulations)` 100 EQUALS JUST 103.8
#ASSERT `art 11(2) to (4): the sum after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `a lump sum for a surviving spouse or civil partner (Schedule 1 to the 2005 Regulations)` 1000 EQUALS JUST 1038
#ASSERT `art 11(2) to (4): the sum after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `an addition for a widow or widower under section 37(1)` 200 EQUALS JUST 207.6
#ASSERT `art 11(2) to (4): the sum after the increase of 3.8 per cent` `a sum not described in art 11(2) to (4)` 100 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Finding F-01: the Order states no rounding for the other 3.8 per cent increases but it states the answer for (1):
-- 17.83 times 1.038 is 18.50754, which is 18.51 to the nearest hundredth, as the text says.
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to the nearest hundredth in the arts 8-19 tests` x MEANS FLOOR (x TIMES 100 PLUS 0.5) DIVIDED BY 100
#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest hundredth in the arts 8-19 tests` (17.83 TIMES (1 PLUS 3.8%)) EQUALS 18.51
-- and the unrounded product is not 18.51 exactly
#ASSERT NOT ((17.83 TIMES (1 PLUS 3.8%)) EQUALS 18.51)

